{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.fixture.process_air_toxics",
    "description": "The `process-crankcase-running` fixture: 1,368 rows of MOVESOutput -- Total Gaseous Hydrocarbons, Carbon Monoxide and Oxides of Nitrogen on BOTH Running Exhaust (process 1) and Crankcase Running Exhaust (process 15), for passenger cars on urban restricted-access roads in Washtenaw County, August, 7am, 2020 -- computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. It ports docs/process-crankcase-running.md end to end and reuses the whole of docs/mixed-onroad.md's spine: the activity chain S1-S9, the cohort structure and the fuel-usage rebase S10-S12, the base rate S13-S14, and the output row S16-S18.\n\nTWO THINGS ARE NEW, AND THEY ARE INDEPENDENT.\n\n(1) THE POLLUTANTS ARE CRITERIA POLLUTANTS. Every earlier onroad fixture rated Total Energy Consumption or a particulate, and neither carries a fuel effect or a humidity correction. These do. The rate table is `emissionRateByAge` and not `emissionRate`, so J22 carries a seventh key pair -- the age group -- because a criteria rate deteriorates. Each base rate is then expanded over the FORMULATIONS the county's fuel supply carries for its fuel type, scaled by `criteriaratio` and `generalfuelratio`, and re-collapsed by market share (adjust.rs:206-262, aggregate.rs:28-45). And NOx alone takes a humidity correction whose equation is selected by a free-text column of a three-row table: k is 1.0216 on gasoline and E85 and 1.00955 on diesel, and dropping it moves every NOx row by more than 2 %.\n\n(2) THE TWO PROCESSES DO NOT SPAN THE SAME KEY SPACE, and that is the whole subject of this rung. `CrankcaseEmissionCalculatorNonPM` is a chained calculator with no rate of its own: a crankcase row is its own pollutant's exhaust row times a tabulated ratio, banded on model year and keyed by (pollutant-process, source type, regulatory class, fuel type). There is no fuelTypeID 9 row in that table and MOVES's join is an INNER one, so the twenty electricity cohorts emit a process-1 row and NO process-15 row: 248 rows per pollutant on process 1 and 208 on process 15. `process-tirewear` could lay its output out as rectangular blocks of a shared cohort rank because all three of its pollutant-processes spanned the same 125 cohorts; three of the six blocks here are twenty cohorts shorter than the other three, so the rank is GLOBAL over the rate relation instead -- `rt_emits` marks the 684 rate rows that reach MOVESOutput and `rt_outputRank` numbers them by an inclusive prefix count (docs/esm-conventions.md 31). No block has to be rectangular, and `pp_emittedCohortCount` states the 124/104 split as an assertion, which is the thing a row count of 1368 cannot make.\n\nTHE FUEL AND HUMIDITY TEMPLATES ARE NOT THIS DOCUMENT'S. `fixtures/process-nox-speciation.esm` reaches the same `BaseRateCalculator` arm and landed all eight of them in lib/adjustments.esm first; this document instantiates them. They were written independently on the two branches, under the same names and with the same bodies, and the reconciliation was to delete the second copy rather than to keep two spellings of `calculateNOxK`. The one template this rung adds is lib/keys.esm's `in_inclusive_range`, and docs/process-crankcase-running.md 4.0 says why it is not `model_year_in_range` renamed.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "fixture",
      "tirewear",
      "pm10",
      "chained-calculator",
      "multi-pollutant"
    ]
  },
