        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "5 rows and THREE levels: 7901 <- 101, 8701 <- 7901, and 2001, 2401 and 2501 <- 8701. MOVES's own statement of which pollutant-process is computed by scaling which other one rather than from a rate of its own. The document reads the chain from here rather than writing `8701 = factor x 7901`, so a run that chained a different pair would need no edit -- and it is what makes the survival rule iterable: `rt_survives1/2/3` apply ONE self-join on (chain input, cohort) three times rather than widening it (docs/process-airtoxics.md \u00a72.6). Only `AirToxicsCalculator` reads this table in MOVES; `HCSpeciationCalculator` has no ChainedTo table at all and speciates a THC block directly, which is why the two stages of this document have different shapes.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "at_crankcaseemissionratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-airtoxics/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__crankcaseemissionratio.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "crankcaseRatio"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_crankcaseemissionratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "572 rows, and the whole of `CrankcaseEmissionCalculatorNonPM`'s arithmetic: crankcase emission = exhaust emission x crankcaseRatio (crankcase_emission.rs:44-56). Keyed by (polProcessID, sourceTypeID, regClassID, fuelTypeID) and BANDED on model year, and both halves of that are load-bearing here. The band: diesel is 0.037 to model year 2000 and exactly 0 from 2001, so two bands are live inside this run's 1980-2020 window; gasoline is 0.33 to 1968 and 0.0132 after, so a document that ignored the band would be 25x wrong on every gasoline cell. The KEY: there is no fuelTypeID 9 row at all, and MOVES's join is an INNER one, so the twenty electricity cohorts emit a process-1 row and no process-15 row. That is the 248/208 split, and it is why this fixture's two processes do not span the same key space.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
