          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The process half: 1 (Running Exhaust) and 15 (Crankcase Running Exhaust)."
        },
        "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "A LEFT JOIN onto runspecchainedto: the exhaust pollutant-process for each of the three crankcase ones, and 0 -- the additive identity, which is no pollutant-process -- for the three that carry a rate of their own. That 0 is what makes the chain term vanish on an unchained row without a branch, and it is also `rt_isChained`'s whole test."
        },
        "ppmy_shortModYrGroupID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "pollutantprocessmodelyear_rows"
          ],
          "description": "modelyeargroup.shortModYrGroupID resolved AT the pollutantprocessmodelyear row. It has to be here rather than on the cohort because a join key column must be one-dimensional and the short group depends on the pollutant-process as well as the model year. All three exhaust pollutant-processes agree here -- model year 2020 maps to short group 40 and 1980 to 1 -- and the three CRANKCASE ones have no `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row at all, so their short group is 0 and their rate join finds nothing. That double suppression is deliberate: a crankcase pollutant-process is not a rate path."
        },
        "rt_ordinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The rate relation's own row ordinal. The relation is the n_runspecpollutantprocess pollutant-processes crossed with the n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype cohort candidate grid -- 3 x 164 = 492 rows, every factor a DISCOVERED extent. It exists because everything the base rate needs is keyed by BOTH, and a join key column has to be one-dimensional (docs/esm-conventions.md 2: tables stay tables)."
        },
        "rt_polProcOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which pollutant-process this rate row is for. Pollutant-process major, so each one occupies a contiguous run of 164 rows."
        },
