        {
          "_comment": "adjust.rs:87-141's two live arms. Both templates return the ADDITIVE term and the `1 +` is written here once, so nothing has to remember which arm returns a factor. Every term is 0 here -- `temperatureadjustment` carries four rows and all four are polProcessID 301 on regClassID 42/46/47/48 for model years 2027-2060, so neither the exact-class nor the regClassID-0 wildcard lookup finds anything -- so the whole temperature half is 1 and the humidity half is NOT: k is 1.0216 on gasoline and E85 and 1.00955 on diesel, and dropping it moves every NOx row by more than 2 %.",
