                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "S15. adjust.rs applies the general fuel ratio, the criteria ratio and the temperature factor to the A/C-ADJUSTED rate as well as to the base rate (they all go through `scale_base_rate`, adjust.rs:296-305) and only then adds `acFactor x acAdj`, so the two factors are common to both terms and the product distributes. It is written factored, and `rt_acFactor` is exactly 0 at this hour, so the two forms are not even floating-point-distinguishable here. The I/M blend and the emission-rate adjustment are the two steps that follow in adjust.rs and both tables are EMPTY in this snapshot (1.3).",
