        {
          "id": "the_fuel_half_of_S15_is_a_criteria_ratio_and_an_unreachable_general_fuel_ratio",
          "description": "S15(g). Each base rate is expanded over the formulations its fuel type is supplied in, scaled, and re-collapsed by market share; every fuel type here is supplied in exactly one formulation at share 1, so `rt_fuelFactor` is just that formulation's `criteriaratio.ratio` and the four values below are the snapshot's own. Electricity has no `criteriaratio` row and takes 1 -- a MISS is a factor of one, not a dropped row. `generalfuelratio` reaches 81 (rate row, formulation) pairs and NOT ONE of them carries a rate, because all 39 of its rows name a crankcase pollutant-process; that zero is the table's entire effect on the answer and is the only way to tell an unreachable step from an unwritten one.",
