        {
          "id": "the_temperature_adjustment_is_all_humidity_at_this_hour",
          "description": "S15's temperature arm, adjust.rs:87-141. `temperatureadjustment` carries four rows and every one is polProcessID 301 on regClassID 42/46/47/48 for model years 2027-2060, so neither the exact-class lookup nor the regClassID 0 wildcard finds anything and every A and B term is 0 -- the temperature half of the factor is exactly 1 on all six pollutant-processes. THE HUMIDITY HALF IS NOT. NOx alone takes k, and k is 1.0216 on gasoline and E85 (CFR 86, reading specific humidity below its 10.71 reference) and 1.00955 on diesel (CFR 1065, reading the water mole fraction); electricity has no `noxhumidityadjust` row and takes 1. Dropping k would move every NOx row by over 2 %, which no per-pollutant sum tolerance in tolerance.toml would catch. The A/C arm is inert, and inert by a CLAMP: the activity term is -0.297 before setup.rs:411 clamps it to [0, 1].",
